1
00:00:02,860 --> 00:00:06,180
FESTIVALS AND CELEBRATIONS

2
00:00:06,500 --> 00:00:12,980
Festivals and celebrations of all kinds have been held everywhere since ancient times.

3
00:00:13,900 --> 00:00:18,600
Most ancient festivals would celebrate the end of cold weather,

4
00:00:18,900 --> 00:00:22,020
planting in spring and harvest in autumn.

5
00:00:22,980 --> 00:00:27,860
Sometimes celebrations would be held after hunters had caught animals.

6
00:00:28,580 --> 00:00:34,120
At that time, people would starve if food was difficult to find,

7
00:00:34,320 --> 00:00:36,940
especially during the cold winter months.

8
00:00:38,260 --> 00:00:40,820
Today's festivals have many origins,

9
00:00:41,420 --> 00:00:42,400
some religious,

10
00:00:42,900 --> 00:00:47,240
some seasonal, and some for special people or events.

11
00:00:49,660 --> 00:00:50,880
FESTIVALS OF THE DEAD

12
00:00:52,540 --> 00:00:58,540
Some festivals are held to honor the dead or to satisfy the ancestors,

13
00:00:58,820 --> 00:01:02,960
who might return either to help or to do harm.

14
00:01:03,780 --> 00:01:06,340
For the Japanese festival, Oban,

15
00:01:06,940 --> 00:01:09,160
people should go to clean graves

16
00:01:09,160 --> 00:01:12,820
and light incense in memory of their ancestors.

17
00:01:13,680 --> 00:01:16,620
They also light lamps and play music,

18
00:01:16,620 --> 00:01:21,260
because they think that this will lead the ancestors back to earth.

19
00:01:22,180 --> 00:01:27,220
In Mexico, people celebrate the Day of the Dead in early November.

20
00:01:28,100 --> 00:01:33,140
On this important feast day, people eat food in the shape of skulls

21
00:01:33,140 --> 00:01:35,560
and cakes with bones on them.

22
00:01:36,140 --> 00:01:39,820
They offer food, flowers, and gifts to the dead.

23
00:01:40,940 --> 00:01:43,220
The Western holiday, Halloween,

24
00:01:43,620 --> 00:01:46,420
also had its origin in old beliefs,

25
00:01:46,420 --> 00:01:49,700
about the return of the spirits of dead people.

26
00:01:50,420 --> 00:01:53,940
It is now a children's festival when they can dress up

27
00:01:53,940 --> 00:01:57,120
and go to their neighbors' homes to ask for sweets.

28
00:01:58,200 --> 00:02:00,660
If the neighbors do not give any sweets,

29
00:02:01,060 --> 00:02:03,820
the children might play a trick on them.

30
00:02:05,820 --> 00:02:07,220
FESTIVALS TO HONOR PEOPLE

31
00:02:08,200 --> 00:02:11,960
Festivals can also be held to honor famous people.

32
00:02:12,560 --> 00:02:17,740
The Dragon Boat Festival in China honors the famous ancient poet,

33
00:02:18,080 --> 00:02:23,540
Chiyuan. In the USA, Columbus Day is in memory of the arrival

34
00:02:23,540 --> 00:02:26,220
of Christopher Columbus in the New World.

35
00:02:27,280 --> 00:02:32,780
India has a national festival on October 2nd to honor Mohandas Gandhi,

36
00:02:33,260 --> 00:02:37,400
the leader who helped gain India's independence from Britain.

37
00:02:38,960 --> 00:02:39,640
HARVEST FESTIVALS

38
00:02:41,140 --> 00:02:45,760
Harvest and Thanksgiving festivals can be very happy events.

39
00:02:46,640 --> 00:02:50,320
People are grateful because their food is gathered for the winter

40
00:02:50,320 --> 00:02:53,200
and the agricultural work is over.

41
00:02:53,880 --> 00:02:57,940
In European countries, people will usually decorate churches

42
00:02:57,940 --> 00:03:03,280
and town halls with flowers and fruits and will get together to have meals.

43
00:03:04,120 --> 00:03:07,500
Some people might win awards for their farm produce,

44
00:03:07,500 --> 00:03:11,980
like the biggest watermelon or the most handsome rooster.

45
00:03:14,020 --> 00:03:16,820
China and Japan have mid-autumn festivals

46
00:03:16,820 --> 00:03:21,900
when people admire the moon and in China enjoy moon cakes.

47
00:03:23,660 --> 00:03:24,300
SPRING FESTIVALS

48
00:03:25,200 --> 00:03:30,760
The most energetic and important festivals are the ones that look forward

49
00:03:30,760 --> 00:03:34,060
to the end of winter and to the coming of spring.

50
00:03:34,700 --> 00:03:37,060
At the spring festival in China,

51
00:03:37,380 --> 00:03:39,940
people eat dumplings, fish and meat

52
00:03:39,940 --> 00:03:43,240
and they give children lucky money in red paper.

53
00:03:44,360 --> 00:03:50,220
There are dragon dances and carnivals and families celebrate the lunar new year together.

54
00:03:51,040 --> 00:03:54,280
Some western countries have very exciting carnivals

55
00:03:54,280 --> 00:03:57,380
which take place 40 days before Easter,

56
00:03:57,680 --> 00:03:59,180
usually in February.

57
00:03:59,880 --> 00:04:02,320
These carnivals might include parades,

58
00:04:02,320 --> 00:04:05,060
dancing in the streets day and night,

59
00:04:05,100 --> 00:04:08,660
loud music and colorful clothing of all kinds.

60
00:04:09,780 --> 00:04:15,540
Easter is an important religious and social festival for Christians around the world.

61
00:04:16,240 --> 00:04:21,000
It celebrates the return of Jesus from the dead and the coming of spring

62
00:04:21,000 --> 00:04:22,240
and new life.

63
00:04:22,840 --> 00:04:26,720
Japan's cherry blossom festival happens a little later.

64
00:04:26,720 --> 00:04:30,400
The country, covered with cherry tree flowers,

65
00:04:30,880 --> 00:04:33,640
looks as though it is covered with pink snow.

66
00:04:34,380 --> 00:04:36,300
People love to get together to eat,

67
00:04:36,460 --> 00:04:38,440
drink and have fun with each other.

68
00:04:39,340 --> 00:04:44,540
Festivals let us enjoy life, be proud of our customs and forget our work

69
00:04:44,540 --> 00:04:45,500
for a little while.
